 How can you apply a custom comparator in a stream pipeline in Java 8?

 1: Simple Custom Comparator

Suppose we have a List<String> and want to sort by string length:
List<String> names = Arrays.asList("Ram", "Shyam", "Alex", "John");

List<String> sorted = names.stream()
                           .sorted((s1, s2) -> Integer.compare(s1.length(), s2.length()))
                           .collect(Collectors.toList());

System.out.println(sorted); //  [Ram, Alex, John, Shyam]


2.Using Comparator.comparing()

More readable and functional:
List<String> sorted = names.stream()
                           .sorted(Comparator.comparing(String::length))
                           .collect(Collectors.toList());

Comparator.comparing() is preferred in modern Java

Can chain multiple sort conditions using .thenComparing()

List<Employee> sortedEmps = employees.stream()
    .sorted(Comparator.comparing(Employee::getDept)
                      .thenComparing(Employee::getSalary))
    .collect(Collectors.toList());



