reduce()

reduce() is a terminal operation that aggregates stream elements into a single result using an identity and accumulator function, 
supporting both sequential and parallel execution.

reduce(U identity, BiFunction<U, ? super T, U>, BinaryOperator<U>)

(Used mainly in parallel streams)

int sum =
    list.stream().reduce(
        0,
        (partial, element) -> partial + element,
        Integer::sum
    );


Identity → initial value
Accumulator → combines element
Combiner → merges partial results


Real Examples
Sum of Numbers
int sum = list.stream().reduce(0, Integer::sum);

Maximum Value
int max = list.stream()
              .reduce(Integer::max)
              .orElse(0);

String Concatenation
String result =
    list.stream().reduce("", String::concat);

Product of Numbers
int product =
    list.stream().reduce(1, (a, b) -> a * b);
    


