 Is it possible to use this and super in a Lambda expression? Explain why or why not.

in a lambda expression, this and super refer to the enclosing class and its superclass respectively,
 because lambdas do not introduce a new scope like anonymous inner classes.
 
Using this in a Lambda Expression
Example
interface Printer {
    void print();
}

class Test {
    String name = "Outer Class";

    void show() {
        Printer p = () -> {
            System.out.println(this.name);
        };
        p.print();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        new Test().show();
    }
}

Output
Outer Class



Using super in a Lambda Expression
Example
class Parent {
    String msg = "Parent";
}

class Child extends Parent {

    void show() {
        Runnable r = () -> {
            System.out.println(super.msg);
        };
        r.run();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        new Child().show();
    }
}

Output
Parent


