 Can a Lambda expression throw an exception? How can you handle exceptions in a Lambda?
 
 yes
 
Unchecked Exceptions (Allowed)

Unchecked exceptions (RuntimeException) can be thrown without restriction.

Runnable r = () -> {
    throw new RuntimeException("Error");
};


✔ Compiles
✔ No throws needed

Checked Exceptions (Compile-Time Restriction)
❌ This will NOT compile
Runnable r = () -> {
    throw new IOException("IO Error");
};


Reason:

Runnable.run() does not declare throws IOException

4. How to Handle Checked Exceptions in Lambda
4.1 Handle Inside Lambda (Most Common)
Runnable r = () -> {
    try {
        throw new IOException("IO Error");
    } catch (IOException e) {
        e.printStackTrace();
    }
};


✔ Works
✔ Clean for small logic


